STANDARDS REFERENCED
--------------------
  CCSDS 131.0-B   TM Synchronization and Channel Coding (public Blue Book)
  CCSDS 401.0-B   Radio Frequency and Modulation Systems
  ITU-R F.1487    HF ionospheric channel simulator (Watterson model)
  SigMF           Signal Metadata Format specification (CC-BY-SA-4.0) —
                  specification text is referenced, not reproduced.

Standards are referenced and implemented from their public descriptions. No
specification text is reproduced in this repository.

KNOWN DEVIATIONS FROM REFERENCED STANDARDS
------------------------------------------
Declared rather than discovered — see README.md "Honest limits":

  * Reed-Solomon uses the conventional (power) basis. CCSDS 131.0-B
    additionally specifies a dual-basis symbol representation, which is not
    implemented. Cartridges declare this as `basis: conventional`.
  * Convolutional puncturing patterns are implemented but have not been
    verified bit-for-bit against the Blue Book.
  * The LDPC family is SHRUTI-defined and fully specified by (n, wc, wr, seed).
    It is not a reproduction of the CCSDS AR4JA or IEEE 802.11n matrices;
    published matrices load through the documented `from_alist` hook.
